        "body": "<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Demo test service now verifies incoming request signatures using HMAC-SHA256 to ensure payload authenticity.\n* **Refactor**\n  * Pull request handling refactored to an action-driven webhook processor with expanded PR metadata and handling for open/close/sync events.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- greptile_comment -->\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Greptile Summary</h3></summary>\n\nThis PR refactors the webhook service to dispatch on PR action type via a `match` statement, fixes the signature verification payload type from `str` to `bytes`, and adds a demo test file. However, the changes introduce several critical defects that leave the entire webhook pipeline broken end-to-end.\n\n- **`git_service.py`**: The whole `CodeReviewService` class is duplicated verbatim (lines 73\u2013140 mirror lines 1\u201368); additionally `process_webhook` calls `self.repository.save_pull_request()` which does not exist on `CodeReviewRepository` (only `create_pull_request` is defined), and `ast.Str` is imported \u2014 a symbol removed in Python 3.12.\n- **`routers/github.py`**: Still calls the deleted `code_review_service.create_pull_request()` method and omits the required `action` keyword argument, so every webhook delivery raises `AttributeError`.\n- **`verify_signature.py`**: The `bytes` type fix here is correct and isolated.\n</details>\n\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Confidence Score: 1/5</h3></summary>\n\nNot safe to merge \u2014 the webhook endpoint is completely non-functional due to multiple broken method call chains.\n\nThe router calls a service method that was deleted in this same PR, and the new service method calls a repository method that has never existed. Both mismatches raise AttributeError on every real webhook delivery, meaning no PR event can be processed at all. The service file is also duplicated verbatim, compounding the maintenance risk.\n\ngit_service.py and routers/github.py both need attention before this is mergeable.\n</details>\n\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Important Files Changed</h3></summary>\n\n\n\n\n| Filename | Overview |\n|----------|----------|\n| apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/service/git_service.py | Refactored service with new process_webhook/action routing, but has three critical defects: entire class duplicated verbatim (lines 73\u2013140), calls non-existent repository.save_pull_request(), and imports removed ast.Str (crashes on Python 3.12+). |\n| apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/routers/github.py | Only whitespace added; still calls the deleted create_pull_request method on the service and omits the required action argument \u2014 every webhook returns a 500. |\n| apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/webhook/verify_signature.py | Correct fix: payload parameter type changed from str to bytes so hmac.new() receives a bytes-like object as required. |\n| apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/repository/git_repository.py | Removed unused SQLAlchemy imports (create_engine, select, Session); no functional change, but still only exposes create_pull_request while the service now calls save_pull_request. |\n| apps/backend/agents/test/demo.py | New test copy of verify_signature with payload typed as str instead of bytes, making hmac.new() raise TypeError on every call. |\n\n</details>\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n<details open><summary><h3>Sequence Diagram</h3></summary>\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant GH as GitHub\n    participant Router as github.py router\n    participant Sig as verify_signature.py\n    participant Svc as CodeReviewService\n    participant Repo as CodeReviewRepository\n\n    GH->>Router: POST /webhook/github (bytes payload)\n    Router->>Sig: verify_signature(headers, payload: bytes, secret)\n    Sig-->>Router: bool (fixed in this PR)\n    Router->>Svc: \"create_pull_request(payload=payload_dict) method deleted - AttributeError\"\n    Note over Router,Svc: Should call process_webhook(payload=..., action=...)\n    Svc->>Svc: _build_pr_data(payload)\n    Svc->>Svc: match action (PullRequestAction)\n    Svc->>Repo: save_pull_request(pr_data) method does not exist - AttributeError\n    Note over Svc,Repo: Repository only defines create_pull_request()\n```\n</details>\n\n\n<!-- greptile_failed_comments -->\n<details open><summary><h3>Comments Outside Diff (2)</h3></summary>\n\n1. `apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/routers/github.py`, line 47 ([link](https://github.com/rajnagani31/codebot/blob/6ad442cf61e36f4ee0f1943d3e776da906203423/apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/routers/github.py#L47)) \n\n   <a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P0\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p0.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Method call doesn't match renamed service method**\n\n   `create_pull_request` no longer exists on `CodeReviewService` \u2014 it was renamed to `process_webhook` in this same PR. Calling the old name raises `AttributeError` on every webhook delivery, making the endpoint completely broken. Additionally, `process_webhook` requires the keyword-only argument `action`, which is also missing from this call site.\n\n2. `apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/routers/github.py`, line 47 ([link](https://github.com/rajnagani31/codebot/blob/2be1a1ca383ca31d8f99994c5efb729032e30403/apps/backend/agents/pr_reviewer_agent/apps/code_reviewer/routers/github.py#L47)) \n\n   <a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P0\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p0.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **Stale method name + missing required argument**\n\n   `create_pull_request` no longer exists on `CodeReviewService` \u2014 it was renamed to `process_webhook` in this same PR. Every incoming webhook delivery will raise `AttributeError` and return a 500. Additionally, `process_webhook` requires the keyword-only argument `action` (sourced from `payload_dict.get(\"action\")`), which is also absent from this call site.\n</details>\n\n<!-- /greptile_failed_comments -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (15): Last reviewed commit: [\"test-1\"](https://github.com/rajnagani31/codebot/commit/e44ee5cedd5b090742c1b37f65016319161cace4) | [Re-trigger Greptile](https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=37279562)</sub>\n\n> Greptile also left **1 inline comment** on this PR.\n\n<!-- /greptile_comment -->",
